===Etymology===
From {{L.}} {{term|plectrum|plēctrum|lang=la}}, from {{AGr.}} '''[[πλήκτρον]]''' {{italbrac|pléktron}} “anything to strike with,  an instrument for striking the lyre, a spear point”, from '''[[πλήσσειν]]''' {{italbrac|pléssein}} “to strike, to smite, to sting”.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|plectra}}

# A small piece of plastic, metal, ivory, etc for [[pluck]]ing the [[string]]s of a [[guitar]], [[lyre]], [[mandolin]], etc.
# {{context|anatomy|zoology}} An [[anatomical]] part resembling a plectrum in shape.

